        "original_id": "25b24c62-cfd4-561b-9d58-ad616cb2491c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Polly Draper, Tim Roth, Nat and Alex Wolff, Boris Pelekh\n- TV Series: Thirtysomething, The Naked Brothers Band\n- Film: The Hit\n- Organizations: ABC, Nickelodeon, Gogol Bordello\n\nFacts:\n- In 1984, Tim Roth received critical acclaim for playing Myron in the film \"The Hit\" and earned his first BAFTA Award nomination for that role.\n- Tim Roth, born on 14 May 1961, is an English actor and director.\n- From 1987 to 1991, Polly Draper first gained recognition for her role in ABC's primetime television drama \"Thirtysomething.\"\n- Nat and Alex Wolff are siblings known for their work on the Nickelodeon television series \"The Naked Brothers Band.\"\n- Polly Draper, who is an actress and the mother of Nat and Alex Wolff, created and produced \"The Naked Brothers Band.\"\n- From 2008 to 2011, Boris Pelekh worked with Nat and Alex Wolff in addition to his work with Gogol Bordello.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
